@@ -683,6 +683,37 @@ retries the same way as any other workflow_streams publisher — see
 the conventional `RETRY` event pattern for surfacing the transition to
 consumers.
 
+For SDK-managed reconstruction, opt in to retry-aware logical output:
+
+```python
+model_params = ModelActivityParameters(
+    streaming_topic="events",
+    streaming_retry_aware=True,
+)
+```
+
+The streaming Activity then publishes `LogicalOutputEvent` envelopes instead
+of raw model events. Every Activity attempt uses the same deterministic logical
+output ID, a generation equal to the Activity attempt, and a fresh delivery
+publisher ID. External subscribers pass the envelopes through
+`LogicalOutputReconstructor(result_type=TResponseStreamEvent)`; a newer
+generation produces a begin update that resets any partial failed attempt,
+chunk updates support incremental rendering, and the terminal update exposes
+the complete result plus an exact offset/hash acknowledgement.
+
+This adapter does not return the successful Activity attempt's terminal receipt
+to Workflow code. Therefore it supports retry-aware reconstruction, but not the
+Workflow-side successful-attempt acknowledgement check shown in the generic
+Workflow Streams example. Applications that require that check must use the
+generic logical output publisher from an Activity whose result includes its
+`LogicalOutputTerminal` receipt.
+
+This option changes the external topic's item type, so existing raw-event
+subscribers must remain in the default mode or be migrated with the publisher.
+`RunResultStreaming.stream_events()` is unchanged and still yields only the
+successful Activity result. See
+[Retry-aware logical output](../workflow_streams/README.md#retry-aware-logical-output).
+
 ## Feature Support
 
 This integration is presently subject to certain limitations.
